Adversarial self-review of the four-file diff found one gap, now fixed. Nothing proved the plan's claim that a base step's rejection passes through the wrappers unchanged. Natively, a swallowed dependencies rejection would turn DEPENDENCY_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH into CHECK_DEPENDENCIES_FAILED, so the altered run would wrongly fail. CY2 gained a sub-row: each of the 3 wrappers hands back the base's own rejection (strictEqual).

Mutation probes, in a /tmp git-archive snapshot outside the repo, pattern ^(CY[1-4]|CF1), baseline 5/5. Each surviving-or-killed result is by AssertionError, not an import or reference error. The snapshot was restored cmp-identical, then removed. Killed (14):
- null-expected match;
- digest-null guard;
- sessions===0;
- any DEPENDENCY_* accepted;
- vm check dropped;
- workspace check dropped;
- seen shared across runs (CF1+CY2);
- no stop at first failure;
- wrapper copies its arg;
- dependencies wrapper swallows a rejection;
- fixed credential;
